<title>UK: Allied London in 18.2 mln stg property sale.</title>
<headline>Allied London in 18.2 mln stg property sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property group Allied London Properties Plc said on Monday it sold two properties for 18.2 million pounds, resulting in a surplus over book value of 1.8 million.</p>
<p>The company said it sold Hagley House in Birmingham for 10 million pounds to Newport Holdings Plc and the former Rackhams department store in Bradford to Schroder Property Exempt Unit Fund for 8.23 million.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
